zlevels-flight-blocked = The floor blocks travel to the other storey.
zlevels-stairs-blocked = The stairs' landing is blocked.
zlevels-demo-created = ZLevels demo created. Grid: {$grid}, map: {$map}. Stairs on the left; shaft, glass and grating on the right.
zlevels-demo-help = Usage: zlevels_demo. Creates an experimental three-storey structure and moves you to the middle storey.
zlevels-gravity-help = Usage: zlevels_gravity on|off. Changes gravity on all floors of the current demo.
zlevels-motion-help = Usage: zlevels_motion vx vy angular. Sets motion and rotation of the current multi-storey demo; 0 0 0 stops it.
zlevels-create-help = Usage: zlevels_create width height. Creates floor 0 with tiles, walls and air, and moves you there. Dimensions: 3 to 256 tiles.
zlevels-add-help = Usage: zlevels_add index. Adds an empty storey to the current structure. Absolute index: -32 to 32; 1 is above floor 0, -1 is below it.
zlevels-link-help = Usage: zlevels_link master-grid floor-grid index. Links an existing grid on another map and aligns it with the master. The master must already use ZLevels; the floor must fit its bounds.
zlevels-go-help = Usage: zlevels_go index. Moves the administrator to the specified floor of the current structure.
zlevels-init-help = Usage: zlevels_init [grid ID]. Enables ZLevels on the current or specified grid, preserving its tiles and contents.
zlevels-init-done = ZLevels enabled. Master grid: {$grid}.
zlevels-init-invalid = Requires a nonempty grid up to 256 by 256 on a map without other Z floors.
zlevels-master-missing = The structure's master grid is missing. Wait for all floor maps to load.
zlevels-stairs-invalid = The staircase needs support and free space inside the structure.
zlevels-stairs-landing-blocked = The staircase's destination is occupied.
zlevels-stairs-unpaired = Staircase disconnected: its other endpoint or floor is missing.
zlevels-stairs-site-guide = Free space for both endpoints on adjacent floors.
construction-name-zlevel-stairs-up = Stairs to the floor above
construction-desc-zlevel-stairs-up = Creates a matching endpoint above. If the floor is missing, creates an empty floor with a landing.
construction-name-zlevel-stairs-down = Stairs to the floor below
construction-desc-zlevel-stairs-down = Creates a matching endpoint below. If the floor is missing, creates an empty floor with a landing.
zlevels-floor-created = Floor {$level} ready. Grid: {$grid}, map: {$map}.
zlevels-invalid-level = Requires a ZLevels master grid and a floor index from -32 to 32.
zlevels-level-exists = A floor with that index already exists in this structure.
zlevels-link-invalid = Requires an unlinked grid on a separate map without other Z floors. Its tiles must fit the master grid's bounds.
zlevels-floor-missing = That floor does not exist in this structure.
ent-ZLevelStairsUp = stairs up
    .desc = Stairs to the storey above. Step onto them to ascend.
ent-ZLevelStairsDown = stairs down
    .desc = Stairs to the storey below. Step onto them to descend.
ent-ActionZLevelAscend = Fly up a storey
    .desc = Fly through an open ceiling using an active jetpack.
ent-ActionZLevelDescend = Fly down a storey
    .desc = Fly through an open floor using an active jetpack.
ent-ActionZLevelGhostAscend = Storey above
    .desc = Move as a ghost to the storey above through solid ceilings.
ent-ActionZLevelGhostDescend = Storey below
    .desc = Move as a ghost to the storey below through solid floors.
